.TH TMUX-CONTINUUM-SAVE-GATE 1 "2026-08-10" "tmux-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmux-continuum-save-gate \- avoid tmux-continuum work until a save is due
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmux-continuum-save-gate
.I x-last-save x-interval save-script
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmux-continuum-save-gate
is the status-interpolation companion to
.BR tmux-continuum-default-server (1).
It prevents frequent
.B status-right
refreshes from invoking tmux-continuum's save script before the configured
deadline.
.PP
The first two arguments are tmux's shell-escaped last-save timestamp and save
interval, each prefixed with a literal
.BR x .
The prefix preserves an empty tmux option as a real shell argument; the command
removes it before validation. Callers should use the exact interpolation
generated by
.BR tmux-continuum-default-server (1).
.PP
An interval of zero exits without saving. Valid numeric values exit without
saving while the deadline remains in the future and execute
.I save-script
when the deadline is due. Missing, malformed, or unusually large state fails
open by executing the native script. Continuum therefore remains authoritative
for ambiguous state instead of losing backups because an optimization could
not prove that a save was unnecessary.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I x-last-save
Continuum's last-save epoch timestamp with the required literal
.B x
prefix.
.TP
.I x-interval
Continuum's save interval in minutes with the required literal
.B x
prefix. Zero disables saving on the current server.
.TP
.I save-script
Executable tmux-continuum save script. A missing or non-executable path is a
quiet no-op because plugin activation may be incomplete.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No save is due, saving is disabled, or the plugin script is unavailable.
.TP
.I other
When a save is due or input is ambiguous, the command replaces itself with
.I save-script
and preserves that script's exit status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR tmux-continuum-default-server (1)
